title: 1876 <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> National Convention
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> Candidate for President
tags: event
view-if: year = 1876 and month = 6
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.third_term_bid = (Q.Winner_68 !== "" && Q.Winner_68 === Q.Winner_72) ? 1 : 0;
!}

= <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> National Convention, 1876

[? if third_term_bid = 1 : President [+ president +] has now won two terms in office, and whispers of an unprecedented third nomination are swirling around the convention hall. No two-term president has ever sought a third term. Some delegates see continuity and strength; others see the makings of a monarchy. ?]

[? if third_term_bid = 0 and president = "Grant" : President Grant, having succeeded to a first full term of his own, could seek renomination, though the party's mood has shifted considerably since his first victory. ?]

[? if third_term_bid = 0 and president = "Wade" : President Wade's **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">radical</span>** tenure has energized the base but alarmed **<span style="color: #B5651D;">Conservatives</span>** and **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderates</span>**  alike. Whether he stands again is very much in question. ?]

[? if third_term_bid = 0 and president = "Chase" : President Chase's **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>** course has frustrated the **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radicals</span>** wing throughout his term, and challengers are already lining up ahead of the convention. ?]

[? if president = "Blaine" or president = "Conkling" : President [+ president +] enters the convention as the incumbent, having taken the office after the last contested floor fight. The party is not entirely settled behind him. ?]

- @ThirdTerm_Push: Push for a historic third term
- @ThirdTerm_Decline: [+ president +] steps aside for a new standard-bearer
- @Incumbent_Renominate: Renominate President [+ president +]
- @Reno_challenge_Incumbent: Support a challenger against [+ president +]
- @Open_Convention_Direct: Let the convention decide from a fresh field

@ThirdTerm_Push
title: Push for a third term
view-if: third_term_bid = 1
choose-if: (radical_strength + moderate_strength + conservative_strength) / 3 >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: The party's factions are too divided to sustain a third-term push.
on-arrival: {!
Q.Candidate = Q.president;
Q.radical_dissent += 10;
Q.moderate_dissent += 6;
Q.conservative_dissent += 12;
Q.liberal_dissent += 15;
Q.dem_relation -= 5;
Q.third_term_won = 1;
!}
go-to: VP_1876

[? if Candidate = "Grant" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Ulysses_S._Grant_1870-1880.jpg" alt="Grant" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Wade" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Benjamin_F_Wade.jpg" alt="Wade" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Chase" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Salmon-P-Chase.webp" alt="Chase" class="face-img"></div> ?]

The convention breaks with a century of precedent. [+ Candidate +] is renominated for a third term amid cheers from loyalists and open dismay from delegates who warn the party is flirting with a one-man rule. The <span class="tooltip-text" title="Democratic" style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrats**</span> press will make the "third term" into a rallying cry all autumn.

@ThirdTerm_Decline
title: Decline a third term
view-if: third_term_bid = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.third_term_won = 0;
!}
go-to: Open_Convention

[+ president +] declines to seek a third term, citing the tradition set by Washington himself. The convention floor opens to a genuinely contested field.

@Incumbent_Renominate
title: Renominate the incumbent
view-if: third_term_bid = 0
choose-if: (president = "Grant" and moderate_strength + conservative_strength >= 35) or (president = "Wade" and radical_strength >= 35) or (president = "Chase" and moderate_strength + conservative_strength >= 40) or (president = "Blaine" or president = "Conkling")
unavailable-subtitle: The party's factions won't hold the line for a renomination fight.
on-arrival: {!
Q.Candidate = Q.president;
Q.radical_dissent += (Q.president === "Wade") ? -5 : 6;
Q.moderate_dissent += (Q.president === "Chase") ? -3 : 3;
Q.conservative_dissent += (Q.president === "Grant") ? -3 : 4;
Q.liberal_dissent += 4;
!}
go-to: VP_1876

[? if Candidate = "Grant" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Ulysses_S._Grant_1870-1880.jpg" alt="Grant" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Wade" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Benjamin_F_Wade.jpg" alt="Wade" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Chase" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Salmon-P-Chase.webp" alt="Chase" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Conkling" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Roscoe_Conkling.jpg" alt="Roscoe Conkling" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Blaine" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/James_G._Blaine.jpg" alt="James Blaine" class="face-img"></div> ?]

The party rallies behind [+ Candidate +] for another term, though enthusiasm is far from unanimous. The **<span style="color: #DAA520;">Liberal Republican</span>** wing continues to eye its own path.

@Reno_challenge_Incumbent
title: Support a challenger to unseat the incumbent
view-if: president = "Grant" or president = "Wade" or president = "Chase" or president = "Blaine" or president = "Conkling"
on-arrival: {!
let incumbentBloc = 0;
if (Q.president === "Wade") incumbentBloc = (Q.radical_strength || 0) + 15;
else if (Q.president === "Chase") incumbentBloc = (Q.moderate_strength || 0) + (Q.conservative_strength || 0) + 15;
else incumbentBloc = (Q.moderate_strength || 0) + (Q.conservative_strength || 0) + (Q.radical_strength || 0) / 2 + 15;

let challengerBloc = (Q.moderate_strength || 0) + (Q.conservative_strength || 0) + (Q.liberal_strength || 0) + (Q.radical_strength || 0) - incumbentBloc + 40;

Q.challenger_beat_incumbent = (challengerBloc > incumbentBloc) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: Open_Convention if challenger_beat_incumbent = 1; incumbent_holds_76 if challenger_beat_incumbent = 0

@incumbent_holds_76

[? if Candidate = "Grant" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Ulysses_S._Grant_1870-1880.jpg" alt="Grant" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Wade" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Benjamin_F_Wade.jpg" alt="Wade" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Chase" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Salmon-P-Chase.webp" alt="Chase" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Conkling" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Roscoe_Conkling.jpg" alt="Roscoe Conkling" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Blaine" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/James_G._Blaine.jpg" alt="James Blaine" class="face-img"></div> ?]

Despite the challenge, [+ president +]'s bloc holds the floor. The incumbent is renominated, though the fight has left the party bruised heading into the fall.

- @VP_1876: Proceed to the Vice Presidential nomination.

@Open_Convention_Direct
go-to: Open_Convention

@Open_Convention

= An Open Field

With no incumbent standing, the convention turns into a genuine contest between the party's rising men. Seven ballots deep, the delegates must choose.

- @Blaine_nominate: James G. Blaine of Maine , the **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>** favorite, tarnished by rumors of railroad corruption
- @Morton_nominate: Oliver P. Morton of Indiana , a **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** stalwart, though his health is failing
- @Conkling_nominate: Roscoe Conkling of New York , the **<span style="color: #B5651D;">Conservatives</span>** machine's man
- @Hayes_nominate: Rutherford B. Hayes of Ohio, a compromise candidate, untainted by scandal

@Blaine_nominate
choose-if: moderate_strength >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>** faction lacks the delegate strength to carry Blaine.
on-arrival: {!
Q.Candidate = "Blaine";
Q.moderate_strength += 4;
Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
Q.conservative_dissent += 5;
Q.radical_dissent += 3;
Q.middle_class_rep += 3;
Q.workers_rep += 1;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/James_G._Blaine.jpg
go-to: VP_1876

Blaine's magnetism carries the **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderates</span>**, though whispers of the Mulligan letters and his railroad dealings will dog him through the general election.

@Morton_nominate
choose-if: radical_strength >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** faction lacks the delegate strength to carry Morton.
on-arrival: {!
Q.Candidate = "Morton";
Q.radical_strength += 4;
Q.radical_dissent -= 4;
Q.moderate_dissent += 4;
Q.conservative_dissent += 6;
Q.freemen_rep += 4;
Q.rural_rep -= 1;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Oliver_Hazard_Perry_Morton.jpg
go-to: VP_1876

Morton, the last true voice of **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** Reconstruction, wins the nomination despite doctors' warnings about the strain of a national campaign.

@Conkling_nominate
choose-if: conservative_strength >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The **<span style="color: #B5651D;">Conservative</span>** faction lacks the delegate strength to carry Conkling.
on-arrival: {!
Q.Candidate = "Conkling";
Q.conservative_strength += 4;
Q.conservative_dissent -= 3;
Q.radical_dissent += 5;
Q.liberal_dissent += 3;
Q.middle_class_rep += 2;
Q.rural_rep += 2;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Roscoe_Conkling.jpg
go-to: VP_1876

Conkling's New York machine delivers him the nomination. Reformers in the party grumble about the spoils system, but the organization behind him is formidable.

@Hayes_nominate
on-arrival: {!
Q.Candidate = "Hayes";
Q.moderate_strength += 2;
Q.radical_dissent -= 2;
Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
Q.liberal_dissent -= 4;
Q.middle_class_rep += 2;
Q.rural_rep += 2;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Rutherford_Hayes.jpg
go-to: VP_1876

Deadlocked between Blaine, Morton, and Conkling, the convention turns to Hayes as a compromise: a three-term Ohio governor with a clean reputation and no enemies to speak of. It is not a nomination of enthusiasm, but of exhaustion.

@VP_1876

= Vice Presidential Nomination

Our candidate is **[+ Candidate +]**.

- @Wheeler_VP: William A. Wheeler (New York)
- @Bristow_VP: Benjamin Bristow (Kentucky)
- @Frelinghuysen_VP: Frederick Frelinghuysen (New Jersey)

@Wheeler_VP
subtitle: Reformer. Little-known but scrupulously honest.
on-arrival: {!
Q.VPCandidate = "Wheeler";
Q.moderate_strength += 2;
Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
Q.radical_dissent += 1;
Q.middle_class_rep += 2;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/19_William_Wheeler_3x4.jpg
go-to: convention_end_1876

Wheeler is a virtual unknown outside New York, but his reputation for honesty balances a ticket increasingly worried about the party's reformist credentials.

@Bristow_VP
subtitle: Reformer. Led the prosecution of the Whiskey Ring; alienates the party machine.
choose-if: liberal_strength + moderate_strength >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The reform wing isn't strong enough to force Bristow onto the ticket.
on-arrival: {!
Q.VPCandidate = "Bristow";
Q.liberal_strength += 3;
Q.liberal_dissent -= 5;
Q.conservative_dissent += 6;
Q.radical_dissent += 2;
Q.middle_class_rep += 4;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Benjamin_Helm_Bristow_Brady_-_Handy_U.S._Secretary_of_Treasury.jpg
go-to: convention_end_1876

Bristow's anti-corruption credentials thrill reformers and reassure **<span style="color: #DAA520;">liberals</span>**, but the party machine, still smarting from the Whiskey Ring prosecutions, is furious.

@Frelinghuysen_VP
subtitle: **<span style="color: #B5651D;">Conservative</span>**. A safe, unremarkable New Jersey senator.
on-arrival: {!
Q.VPCandidate = "Frelinghuysen";
Q.conservative_strength += 3;
Q.conservative_dissent -= 3;
Q.radical_dissent += 2;
Q.rural_rep += 2;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Frederick_T._Frelinghuysen_-_Brady-Handy.jpg
go-to: convention_end_1876

Frelinghuysen brings no particular strength to the ticket, but no particular liability either; a safe hand chosen to avoid further factional strife.

@convention_end_1876

= The Ticket is Set

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican Party**</span> will enter the 1876 election with **[+ Candidate +]** for President and **[+ VPCandidate +]** for Vice President.

[? if third_term_bid = 1 and third_term_won = 1 : The third-term nomination has handed the <span class="tooltip-text" title="Democratic Party" style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrats**</span>  their central campaign issue before the race has even begun. ?]

[? if liberal_dissent >= 25 : The **<span style="color: #DAA520;">Liberal Republican</span>** wing is deeply unhappy with the ticket, and turnout among reform-minded voters may suffer. ?]

[? if radical_dissent >= 25 : **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical Republicans</span>** are openly grumbling. Their lukewarm support could suppress turnout among freedmen and Northern reformers alike. ?]

[? if liberal_dissent < 25 and radical_dissent < 25 : The party appears reasonably unified behind the ticket, all things considered. ?]